## TRAP 9 — SKIPPED IS NOT PASSED (a check surface reporting green for work never run)

A **CONFLICTING** PR cannot have its merge ref built, so GitHub reports the ENTIRE matrix as
`skipped`. Any summary counting "not failing" as green reads that as a pass. Lane 1C caught itself
about to report CI green off those skips. On #2035's head the skipped rows included
`Test (Python ${{ matrix.python-version }})` — an UNEXPANDED matrix template, i.e. the duplicate
run's placeholder.

**Always separate success from skipped:**
`gh api .../commits/<sha>/check-runs --jq '[.check_runs[]]|group_by(.conclusion)|map("\(.[0].conclusion): \(length)")'`

